{"title": "AI agent communication protocols compared: MCP vs A2A vs ACP vs ANP vs Pilot — which fits your stack?", "slug": "direct-communication-protocols-ai-agents-guide", "section": "blog", "description": "Compare five AI agent communication protocols across transport, discovery, trust, reachability, and application semantics to choose a complementary stack.", "seoTitle": "AI Agent Communication Protocols Compared | Pilot Protocol", "author": "Pilot Protocol editorial team", "publishedAt": "2026-06-29T12:00:00.000Z", "tags": ["comparison", "mcp", "a2a", "acp", "anp", "protocols"], "content": {"root": {"type": "root", "children": [{"type": "quote", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "TL;DR:", "format": 1, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}, {"type": "text", "text": " These protocols cover different parts of the stack. MCP handles tool and resource access. A2A, ACP, and ANP define application-level agent interaction or discovery. Pilot operates at the network layer with retained-identity addressing, encrypted UDP tunnels, traversal, and peer trust. This guide compares the layers and shows where they compose.", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1}, {"type": "horizontalrule", "version": 1}, {"type": "heading", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Why AI agent communication protocols matter", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "tag": "h2"}, {"type": "paragraph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Agents fail to connect for predictable reasons: they sit behind NAT, they restart and change IP addresses, they span clouds with no shared network, or they have no way to verify peer identity before accepting a task. The set of ", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}, {"type": "text", "text": "AI agent communication protocols", "format": 1, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}, {"type": "text", "text": " that emerged between 2024 and 2026 each solves a different slice of this problem. Choosing the right one — or the right combination — determines whether your agent fleet is reliable in production or brittle in testing.", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "textFormat": 0, "textStyle": ""}, {"type": "paragraph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "This comparison covers five protocols: MCP, A2A, ACP, ANP, and Pilot Protocol. Each is described fairly on its own terms. Where they overlap, we note it. Where they compose well, we show how.", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "textFormat": 0, "textStyle": ""}, {"type": "horizontalrule", "version": 1}, {"type": "heading", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Protocol comparison: MCP vs A2A vs ACP vs ANP vs Pilot", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "tag": "h2"}, {"type": "table", "children": [{"type": "tablerow", "children": [{"type": "tablecell", "headerState": 1, "colSpan": 1, "rowSpan": 1, "backgroundColor": null, "children": [{"type": "paragraph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Protocol", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "textFormat": 0, "textStyle": ""}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1}, {"type": "tablecell", "headerState": 1, "colSpan": 1, "rowSpan": 1, "backgroundColor": null, "children": [{"type": "paragraph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Layer", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "v